NAME
       udevadm - control udev, the service that names devices

SYNOPSIS
       udevadm settle
       udevadm trigger
       udevadm info DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       udev creates the device files in /dev and the links under
       /dev/disk/by-uuid, by-label and by-path when the kernel finds hardware
       or a new partition. udevadm talks to it.

       settle waits until udev has handled every pending event, so that new
       device names exist before the next command uses them (useful right
       after making partitions in a script). trigger asks udev to go through
       all devices again. info prints what udev knows about a device.

EXAMPLES
           parted -s /dev/vdb mkpart data xfs 1MiB 1GiB
           udevadm settle
           ls -l /dev/disk/by-partlabel/

SEE ALSO
       lsblk(8), blkid(8), partprobe(8)
